 "notes": "BBN 4He exclusion (orange region, left panel of Fig. 1) from the axion e-print figure gdFinal.pdf, extracted from the vector paths. Axes calibrated from tick marks; g_d axis verified against the paper's QCD-axion line, confirming the plotted convention g_d = e*(2.4e-16 cm)/f_a ~ 3.7e-3 GeV^-1/f_a (dn = g_d a in natural units), matching the canonical L = -(i/2) g_d a Nbar sigma_munu gamma_5 N F^munu. The paper draws the bound as a thick line whose width reflects the ~40% uncertainty in g_d (eq. 16); I report the geometric center of that band (edges differ by ~factor 2.3), so the curve is within ~1.5x of either edge. Text bound: f_a m_a > 1.3e-9 GeV^2 for m_a > 1e-16 eV (delta Yp/Yp < 10%, Yp 95% CL range from PDG), scaling as f_a m_a > 1.8e-9 GeV^2 (m_a/1e-16 eV)^{3/4} for ultralight m_a; the extracted curve shows the corresponding slope-1 and slope-1/4 regimes. Cosmological bound (mean DM density from Planck), so no local-density rescaling. CASPEr curves in the right panel are projections and are not reported.",
